{"skill":{"slug":"discord-voice","displayName":"Discord Voice"},"version":{"version":"0.1.6","createdAt":1771367678507,"changelog":"discord-voice 0.1.6\n\n- No code or documentation changes detected in this version.\n- Functionality and configuration remain identical to the previous release.","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","size":1692,"sha256":"9095fc83bbbc99425e9f07b08b57d675987dd2cce57726ddf30a8714e6bee4cc","contentType":null},{"path":".oxlintrc.json","size":3742,"sha256":"a932348c956505fc9eabb7ff3a8dfe08ee639bc900cdf7d54a171d8bff31aff6","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"openclaw.plugin.json","size":11531,"sha256":"3662e764208928d447d40dd4526d1c01f6bc0489dd17de5df9d1955a826ea5e7","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"README.md","size":22646,"sha256":"1f6834d7115c7743a9ae52129d585b53f453da8440b46935609ce0a8e97ffdfd","contentType":null},{"path":"package-lock.json","size":442320,"sha256":"c1c0f4c9e88b102a81136f6f5e8877c498f0b469a9201cf3cc73219a0d7d46d2","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"package.json","size":1804,"sha256":"d2d89a00c1d9748a838fb0ec516b7ec4b808b9d0b42b008a0e56b3da4390f09c","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"scripts/smoke-test.mjs","size":5890,"sha256":"80a5067056256f59a8a9450ce54a75de6d5d98c50a45995b8959fdd403e2f8e9","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":".github/workflows/ci.yml","size":345,"sha256":"ba54afe8d5726a6aa699a6b245034370a42248924e05b64c662eabe0fc200123","contentType":null},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":9028,"sha256":"cb946aa07567759b4f0f91cc68c9f9be69090dd0d65e571e686f2b3a2ba50029","contentType":null},{"path":"tsconfig.json","size":532,"sha256":"64edfc3384483ab069ca33934c02660430fafb32803dc3e266d1a15d3f11fb37","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"index.ts","size":41133,"sha256":"d1758e931719a0dd441978e044ba9818cb3efb8a531f8f61f7b9afe37361e84a","contentType":null},{"path":".oxfmtrc.json","size":107,"sha256":"0ffa3b4f0c0c7281f9cfa10f1aa7a95ee813dbd85c248ffcded1ab9cd681cbea","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"clawdbot.plugin.json","size":8708,"sha256":"f440c3659cab14e3880179c328db21f09be7d91c5eaf18658f246fe0bab03cab","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"SECURITY.md","size":3464,"sha256":"1f5df9626db0b8beefe369a7895fbe327defd78509150bf8c17bf11f24b1037c","contentType":null},{"path":"src/stt.ts","size":16722,"sha256":"9115cec17623309f6731215e631459dd14cd52a632f3310e3a829d3e1269da81","contentType":null},{"path":"src/streaming-tts.ts","size":7040,"sha256":"3058ab762ff680e712b9cd782bdbadc8b8963c6e0dddb0871c0314f8ce9eb32c","contentType":null},{"path":"src/tts.ts","size":12079,"sha256":"f3478300e34234d0f309cba798a4b191c902d58252d71c0c064cd5dffa95cc78","contentType":null},{"path":"src/constants.ts","size":727,"sha256":"3e0c87b54fa6221a59c1073e2a25d3d9d55befbc568fdb6e27179b11d4c89c7c","contentType":null},{"path":"src/voice-connection.ts","size":47841,"sha256":"5fe61d8f7d9ec7c9a22710e019a13732c812c433a3aa31d39a1144dd8f4f98af","contentType":null},{"path":"src/config.ts","size":27598,"sha256":"8d63b4ee5055309ee3291f8e834ff24e19c2f0e4939c05c8e228d0780d665c2a","contentType":null},{"path":"src/core-bridge.ts","size":6578,"sha256":"5d17feda4485a65d2e391111a370be421f5865be7867015748ad27fc72aae22f","contentType":null},{"path":"src/streaming-stt.ts","size":11852,"sha256":"2f4a4791ed11977de310cac36ee9d94010ca4471020649673dc2a3dbd65fd2bf","contentType":null},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2610,"sha256":"66dc64ee5964e16fefcea86462e7aa8e9945d9e884b0d4d87aec239fb5ee528f","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789021842589,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"825ffd9bb19da9024a5aad60e631a09e494c78c87f8e71f73cb9a9d783393a4c","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/825ffd9bb19da9024a5aad60e631a09e494c78c87f8e71f73cb9a9d783393a4c","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: discord-voice\nVersion: 0.1.6\n\nThe OpenClaw Discord Voice plugin is designed with strong security considerations. It implements robust sanitization for all user-controlled inputs before they are used in agent prompts or file paths, specifically preventing prompt injection via user IDs and path traversal for custom sound files. The dynamic loading of the core OpenClaw extension API is performed with integrity checks, verifying the package name and resolving paths securely. While the plugin connects to various external STT/TTS APIs and a configurable local Wyoming Whisper server, these network interactions are for its stated purpose and API keys are handled via configuration or environment variables, not directly from user input. No evidence of intentional harmful behavior, such as data exfiltration to unauthorized endpoints or backdoor installation, was found.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160058439},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":94,"checkedAt":1789021842589},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill largely does what it claims, but by default anyone in a joined Discord voice channel can drive a full OpenClaw agent and share persisted context, so it needs review before use.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Discord voice permissions and named provider API keys are purpose-aligned, but the skill can transmit speech to external STT/TTS providers, use AWS credential resolution for Polly, log transcript content, and accept remote Wyoming STT endpoints over unauthenticated TCP.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Installation is conventional npm plus documented system packages, but the lockfile includes a broad OpenClaw peer dependency graph, install-script packages, a git+ssh dependency, and a package.json/package-lock version mismatch. No malicious install behavior was found in the artifact itself.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The docs disclose that allowedUsers empty means all users, but they do not clearly scope voice-originated requests to a restricted agent profile, require an allowlist, or require participant consent before recording, transcription, third-party processing, and tool-enabled agent execution.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The plugin registers a background service and heartbeat/reconnect timers as expected for voice operation. More importantly, agent sessions are persisted under a guild-only session key, so different users and channels in the same guild can share context and influence later interactions.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is coherent: join Discord voice, record speech, transcribe it, route it to the agent, synthesize a reply, and play it back. The material concern is that transcripts are passed to runEmbeddedPiAgent with the prompt saying the agent has all normal tools and skills, while the default allowedUsers setting permits all speakers in joined channels.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only in trusted Discord servers or channels, configure allowedUsers explicitly, and run voice-originated requests with a restricted agent/tool profile. Tell participants that speech may be recorded, logged, transcribed, sent to providers, and used as agent input. Prefer local or TLS-protected STT/TTS paths, avoid remote Wyoming TCP unless secured by a trusted tunnel, and audit/update the npm lockfile before production use.","findings":"[T05] unexpected: Confirmed in artifact: empty allowedUsers returns true and the voice transcript is sent to a normal tool-enabled OpenClaw agent. This is not evidence of malicious intent, but it is overbroad by default.\n[T05] unexpected: Confirmed in artifact: the session key is scoped to discord:voice:<guildId>, not user or channel, so cross-user and cross-channel context sharing is a real design risk.\n[T09] unexpected: Confirmed in artifact: full transcribed speech and a response excerpt are written at info level. Logging metadata would be expected; logging voice content by default is not necessary for the core purpose.\n[T09] expected: Confirmed in artifact: Wyoming STT sends audio over node:net TCP. Remote STT is purpose-aligned when configured, but confidentiality and integrity are under-documented and should be treated as insecure unless tunneled or loopback-only.\n[T08] unexpected: Confirmed in lockfile: a transitive peer path includes a git+ssh dependency and install-script components. No malicious payload was found, but it increases installation supply-chain risk.\n[SC4] unexpected: The lockfile contains the reported dependency versions. Several appear transitive or peer-related rather than direct imports of the Discord voice code, so this supports supply-chain caution rather than a malicious verdict.\n[SC6] expected: The oxlint package appears in devDependencies as a linter command and is consistent with the package scripts; this looks like a false-positive typosquatting signal.\n[E2] expected: The code reads specific named environment variables such as OPENAI_API_KEY, ELEVENLABS_API_KEY, and DEEPGRAM_API_KEY. This is disclosed and purpose-aligned, not bulk environment harvesting.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: Confirmed in docs: speech recording, transcription, and provider use are described, but there is no clear privacy or consent section near the top. This is a material deployment risk for Discord voice channels.\n[PE2] expected: The sudo commands are installation prerequisites for ffmpeg and native build tools, not runtime privilege escalation by the skill. Users should still install system packages through normal administrator review.\n[P9] expected: The flagged whitespace is table alignment in README configuration rows. I found no hidden prompt-injection content associated with it.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789021842589}}}}}